1. RIGHT TO DOWNLOAD & USE
   Any user or developer may download, install, and run OpenCode Studio and its
   bundled tools free of charge on any personal or development machine.

2. RIGHT TO REPORT ISSUES & BUGS
   Users and developers are encouraged to submit bug reports, auto-captured
   error diagnostics, and feature requests via GitHub Issues at:
   https://github.com/vaasiraq-art/opencode-studio/issues

3. RIGHT TO EDIT LOCALLY & SUBMIT CONTRIBUTIONS
   Developers may fork, inspect, and edit the source code locally to fix bugs,
   add providers, improve routing strategies, or add skills/plugins, and submit
   Pull Requests back to the official repository.

4. OFFICIAL DEPLOYMENT & RELEASE AUTHORITY
   Official releases, signed installers (.exe), and main-branch deployments of
   OpenCode Studio are reviewed, approved, and published exclusively by the
   repository maintainer (vaasiraq-art) on:
   https://github.com/vaasiraq-art/opencode-studio

   Redistributing modified builds under the name "OpenCode Studio" as official
   releases without prior maintainer approval is not permitted.

